  "content": {
    "id": "p18-q20",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "20",
    "prompt": "A small rectangular block of land has a perimeter of 100 m and an area of 225 m².\nFind the dimensions of the block of land.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$5\\text{ m}$ by $45\\text{ m}$; use $x(50-x)=225$.",
      "worked": "Let the dimensions be $x$ m and $y$ m, with $x,y>0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}2x+2y&=100\\\\y&=50-x\\end{align*}$$\nUsing $A=xy$:\n$$\\begin{align*}225&=x(50-x)\\\\x^2-50x+225&=0\\\\(x-5)(x-45)&=0\\\\x&=5\\text{ or }45\\end{align*}$$\nThe corresponding values of $y$ are $45$ and $5$. The dimensions are $5\\text{ m}$ by $45\\text{ m}$.\nCheck: $2(5+45)=100\\text{ m}$ and $5\\times45=225\\text{ m}^2$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 85
  },
